#%PAM-1.0
# Nested lock screen tests only (BUCHHWIN_NESTED=1) and
# tests/qml/LockScreenTest.qml: asks for a password and accepts exactly one,
# "lock-test-password". Any other answer, an empty one included, fails the
# way a wrong password does at a real login - PAM_AUTH_ERR from pam_deny, the
# lock's PamResult.Failed - so a password lost on its way from the field to
# PAM shows here, where test-permit takes it. (test-deny fails as a system
# error instead.) pam_exec hands the password over with its terminating NUL,
# which ends a line for grep -z.
auth     [success=1 default=ignore]  pam_exec.so expose_authtok quiet /usr/bin/grep -qxzF lock-test-password
auth     requisite                   pam_deny.so
auth     required                    pam_permit.so
account  required                    pam_permit.so
